pharyngeal dysphagia, incorporating various therapeutic measures.", "FAMILIARES:The term \"FAMILIARES\" refers to family members who play a crucial role in the care and support of patients. They are individuals related to the patient and can provide both emotional and practical assistance, particularly during the rehabilitation process for conditions such as oropharyngeal dysphagia. In cases involving specific disorders like galactosemia, family members may have a history of the condition, which can significantly influence screening and treatment decisions. Additionally, family members are often consulted for consent in situations where the patient is unable to make decisions for themselves. Their proximity to the patient allows them to have a substantial impact on treatment choices and consent processes, especially in instances of the patient's incapacity. Overall, family members are integral to the patient's healthcare journey, providing support and facilitating important decisions regarding treatment and consent.", "EVALUACIÓN CLÍNICA:Clinical evaluation is a comprehensive assessment of the patient's medical history, cognitive abilities, and swallowing function to inform treatment planning.", "PACIENTE CON DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA:El paciente con disfagia orofaríngea es una persona que presenta dificultades para deglutir, lo que puede afectar su nutrición y calidad de vida.", "TÉCNICAS COMPENSADORAS:Las técnicas compensadoras son métodos que permiten al paciente comer algunos alimentos por vía oral, mejorando los síntomas de la disfagia de manera inmediata.", "EVALUACIÓN CLÍNICA E INSTRUMENTAL:La evaluación clínica e instrumental es un proceso necesario para determinar las características adecuadas del bolo alimenticio para el paciente con disfagia.", "MODIFICACIONES EN EL VOLUMEN, TEXTURA Y VISCOSIDAD DEL BOLO:Las modificaciones en el volumen, textura y viscosidad del bolo son técnicas utilizadas para facilitar la deglución en pacientes con disfagia orofaríngea.", "FLEXIÓN CERVICAL:A recommended posture for patients to protect the airway during swallowing by lowering the chin or tucking it in.", "EXTENSIÓN CERVICAL:A posture where the patient raises the chin to facilitate the passage of food from the mouth to the pharynx.", "ROTACIÓN DE LA CABEZA:A technique where the patient rotates the head towards the affected side to direct the food bolus towards the healthy side.", "INCLINACIÓN LATERAL DE LA CABEZA:A posture where the patient tilts the head towards the stronger side to assist in swallowing."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}